    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "KG → package → distribution → portal",
      "prov:value": "**This is the shape of that path**, and it is\nwritten as a pattern because the IRIS replica built it by accident first and nothing\nnamed it, so the next instance would have rebuilt it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "KG → package → distribution → portal",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-20:\n\n> *\"this is doing webportal mockup as part of CRDM of kg. based on custom\n> assets with need to defin a data ingestion pirpeline (subject ot\n> operational/deployment constrsaints, $, network traffic, graph seize etc),\n> from KG into a public portal. this is ecample creating a CDN to sit behind\n> moodle.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "The one distinction that makes the rest fall out",
      "prov:value": "`PUBLICATION_HOSTS` in `schemas/kg/cat-harness.ts` is `github-pages`,\n`local-server`, `jurisdiction-endpoint`, `none` — axis 3 of\n[`deployment-topologies`](../../../docs/proposals/deployment-topologies.md).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "docs/proposals/deployment-topologies.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The one distinction that makes the rest fall out",
      "prov:value": "Getting that wrong has a specific cost, and it is the cost `xies` calls *\"EXTREME\ncare in URL handling\"*: if the CDN is modelled as the host, the published URL\nbecomes the CDN's URL, and the day the CDN changes every citation breaks."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "The one distinction that makes the rest fall out",
      "prov:value": "**Do not add a CDN value to `PUBLICATION_HOSTS`.** A fifth value there without\na row in the proposal is a vocabulary nobody agreed, and this one would also be\nwrong."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the deployment decides, and the pipeline must not",
      "prov:value": "Three decisions belong to the deployment. The owner named all three as\nconstraints rather than as preferences, and a diagram or a script that picks\none is asserting a decision nobody made."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the deployment decides, and the pipeline must not",
      "prov:value": "**1. The ingestion method is UNDETERMINED.** Owner, verbatim: *\"ingestion\nmethod not determined.\"*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the deployment decides, and the pipeline must not",
      "prov:value": "Owner: *\"need hosted git or suitable versioned storage for graph network like\nKG."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the deployment decides, and the pipeline must not",
      "prov:value": "**3. The distribution transport.** GitHub Pages is a tool choice — `xies`\ncarries that verbatim, and since 2026-09-30 it is literally one: the `gh-pages`\nTool, satisfying the general [`render-kg-to-cdn`](../../process/workflow/render-kg-to-cdn.md)\nstep — and so is jsDelivr, Cloudflare, or an object store.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The constraints the choice is made under",
      "prov:value": "Owner: *\"subject ot operational/deployment constrsaints, $, network traffic,\ngraph seize etc.\"*"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The constraints the choice is made under",
      "prov:value": "A figure taken from a vendor's documentation is a *quoted* figure and\nsays so; one taken from a chat message is neither, and the IRIS replica catalogue\ncarries the worked example — every note in a branch said \"0.7 TB\", sourced from\na chat message, and the measured figure was about half."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Trust: GDHCN, distributed as WHO SMART Trust DID trustlists",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-20, in two messages: **`propsal signing = GDHCN`**, then\n**the trust IG**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Trust: GDHCN, distributed as WHO SMART Trust DID trustlists",
      "prov:value": "The second names where the first is specified — the\n[WHO SMART Trust Implementation Guide](https://smart.who.int/trust)\n(`smart.who.int.trust`, FHIR R5, v1.8.0 at the time of reading, support address\n`gdhcn-support@who.int`)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The correction this made to an earlier draft of this skill",
      "prov:value": "### The correction this made to an earlier draft of this skill"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What that settles, and it is the design's own argument back at it",
      "prov:value": "**Three of the four questions this section used to carry are now answered** —\nonboarding (a documented process, `concepts_onboarding.md`, with its own\n[checklist](https://smart.who.int/trust/concepts_onboarding_checklist.html)),\ncaching (native to the design), and the envelope (a trustlist is keys; the\nenvelope is elsewhere, and for a document package is unsettled)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/kg-to-portal.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "What that settles, and it is the design's own argument back at it",
      "prov:value": "**Nothing about GDHCN is\nwritten here from general knowledge** — that is the `r1lz` rule, and the first\ndraft of this section broke it in exactly the way the rule predicts: it was\nplausible, it was confident, and the part it got wrong (envelope versus key\ndistribution) was the part that decides what stage 4 is."
    },
    {
